---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2026-08-31";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use | Category Checker" description="Terms for using the Category Checker tool.">
  <section class="wrap flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-[36px] font-medium leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.5px] text-heading">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-[13px] text-fg-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Acceptance</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      By using Category Checker, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, don't use the tool.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Category Checker is provided "as is," free of charge, with no guarantee of accuracy, availability, or fitness for a
      particular purpose. Provider results — including the currently mocked sample data — should always be confirmed
      against the provider's own console before being relied on for a security or access-control decision.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Independence</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Category Checker is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Microsoft,
      Fortinet, Cisco, Zscaler, or Netskope. Their product and company names are trademarks of their respective owners.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Don't use Category Checker to abuse, overload, or attempt to circumvent rate limits on this site or any third-party
      provider it queries.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Changes</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      These terms may change as the tool evolves. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance of the updated
      terms.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
